counterexample:
Usernames or open text inputs that cannot be represented by a closed set of variants:
```rust
struct UserProfile {
    display_name: String,
}
```

fix:
Represent the states using a compile-time checked `enum`.
```rust
enum PermissionState {
    Requested,
    Approved,
    Denied,
}

struct SystemPermission {
    state: PermissionState,
}
```
